<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21823" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">impătĭentĭa</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inp-</span></b> ), ae,
			f.
		impatiens. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Unwillingness</i> or <i>inability to
				bear</i> any thing, <i>want of endurance</i>, <i>impatience</i> (post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(a).</b> With <i>gen.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nauseae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Calig. 23 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">frigorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 23, 27, § 77</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aetas extrema, fessa mente, retinet silentii
					impatientiam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					4, 52</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caritatis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 13, 21</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Veneris,</span>”
				i. e. <i>impatience</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 2, p. 121</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b>
			<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ne ipse visendo ejus tormenta ad impatientiam
					dilaberetur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 15, 63</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">culpa impatientiae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					1, 13, 3</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Insensibility</i>, <i>impassibility</i>, <i>apathy</i>, as a transl. of
			the Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπάθεια</span>, <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep.
				9, 1</span></i>. </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
